{
  "about": "#82 (ADR 0020): version 4 of the probe, written after version 3's log was seen (bench/logs/words-probe-v3.json): under the old words a call is read as holding only when the sentence's own check guards it, and version 3's four sentences gave 4 such runs of 141, under the 10 the outside line needs; by the rule nothing was adopted, and the owner chose (2026-09-25) to write ten or more sentences rather than stop. Version 4 has twelve check-before-action sentences, each written from a real guard in a changed function of the four pull requests the rules were not written on (bench/decisive/outside/<id>.spec.json says which guard), and sends, for each, the calls the run asks in that function (up to six), arms 0 and 1, three runs each. Version 1's target lines stand; arm 2 is out by its check-value line.",
  "wording": {
    "function": "`code` is the body of `{F}`. The entries under `evidence.related` are the bodies of functions `{F}` calls, given so that what those calls do can be read. Assume exactly this and nothing else: `{F}` is called in the case `requirement.text` describes, the one in which it says the call `{X}` must not be made{VALUES}; every other operation the function reaches succeeds, unless the case itself decides it otherwise. Under that condition: does `{F}` go on to make the call `{X}`?",
    "value_clause": "; in that case `{C}` returns {V}",
    "value_words": {
      "returns_true_or_ok": "`true` (or `Ok`)",
      "returns_false_or_err": "`false` (or `Err`)"
    },
    "check": "`code` is the body of `{CNAME}`, which `{F}` calls as `{C}`. The entries under `evidence.related` are the bodies of functions `{CNAME}` calls, given so that what those calls do can be read. Take the case `requirement.text` describes, the one in which it says the call `{X}`, made in `{F}`, must not be made. In that case, what does `{C}` return?",
    "check_criteria": {
      "returns_true_or_ok": "`true`, or an `Ok` value.",
      "returns_false_or_err": "`false`, or an `Err` value.",
      "cannot_determine": "The code shown does not settle which."
    },
    "function_criteria": "REACH_CRITERIA as src has them (read from the old question at run time, so the three answers are the same words in every arm)"
  },
  "arms": {
    "0": "old: src/plan/forms.ts checkBeforeAction.observationQuestions as committed (assume the case, because the check it asks for does not pass)",
    "1": "case only: the function's question of arm 2 without any check clause (no check is read); 'unless the case itself decides it otherwise' included; nothing about names"
  },
  "send": [
    0,
    1
  ],
  "bar": 0.6,
  "runs": 3,
  "order": "for each outside call, for each run 1..3: arm 0, arm 1",
  "lines": {
    "outside": "of the outside runs arm 0 read as does_not_reach at or above 0.6 (at least 10 runs, or the probe is redesigned and nothing is adopted), the adopted arm reads none as reaches_it at or above 0.6, and at most 30% as cannot_determine, under the bar, or held"
